      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140421_18180298_0068.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140421_18180298_0068&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140421_18180298_0068.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140421_18181067_0069.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140421_18181067_0069&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140421_18181067_0069.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: Mother Gowin, To: Jeanette Knox Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Morrisonville, Illinois on December 31, 1917&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mrs. E.H. Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Pearl, Illinois&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Morrisonville, Illinois Dec 31, 1917&lt;br&gt;
Dear Mother Chandler,&lt;br&gt;
I wish you many happy birthdays. Hoping you are all well and wish for a very happy holiday.&lt;br&gt;
Lovingly yours,&lt;br&gt;
Mother Gowin&lt;/p&gt;</description>
